{"h":3209,"lines":[{"t":"Test 1","w":0.064077669779459626,"x":0.085436893573053327,"y":0.043604650906894915,"h":0.017454538909817074,"c":1},{"h":0.021576015674436677,"y":0.091471269776993269,"c":1,"x":0.087160805654185464,"w":0.30916803995768227,"t":"READING PASSAGE 2"},{"t":"You should spend about 20 minutes on Questions 14-26, which are based on Reading","x":0.087273695616459576,"h":0.023577468491788989,"y":0.13003947103336777,"w":0.82353597005208334,"c":1},{"x":0.087047175619895917,"w":0.16950503031412759,"y":0.14966918678939911,"c":1,"h":0.021652692277854935,"t":"Passage 2 below."},{"y":0.19622093001278795,"x":0.19223301103449367,"t":"Forest management in Pennsylvania, USA","w":0.62524271647135421,"h":0.030570346915461899,"c":1},{"w":0.76722340901692698,"c":1,"t":"How managing low-quality wood (also known as low-use wood) for bioenergy can","x":0.12027799085294816,"h":0.022135730398778253,"y":0.23905521889073278},{"h":0.019494209408388641,"c":1,"t":"encourage sustainable forest management","x":0.30083026543702557,"w":0.40806732177734367,"y":0.25863225601953821},{"w":0.017475727399190261,"h":0.014534883112922281,"y":0.65406976762474045,"x":0.089320388646683194,"c":1,"t":"C"},{"y":0.29469860186206542,"w":0.75933649698893235,"t":"A tree's 'value' depends on several factors including its species, size, form, condition,","h":0.021202786169319476,"c":1,"x":0.10673647197812443},{"t":"quality, function, and accessibility, and depends on the management goals for a given","y":0.31338002588155733,"w":0.72841089884440113,"c":1,"h":0.022715794928720001,"x":0.1319230181500391},{"c":1,"h":0.022585609174591736,"y":0.3309956093983184,"w":0.78460851033528645,"t":"forest. The same tree can be valued very differently by each person who looks at it. A large,","x":0.13195117331969622},{"x":0.13382470585399819,"w":0.78277628580729164,"t":"straight black cherry tree has high value as timber to be cut into logs or made into furniture,","y":0.34999941379601607,"h":0.022630419389481071,"c":1},{"t":"but for a landowner more interested in wildlife habitat, the real value of that stem (or trunk)","y":0.37063953515547965,"w":0.7825242614746093,"h":0.0188953482844747,"x":0.13203884013316658,"c":1},{"c":1,"t":"may be the food it provides to animals. Likewise, if the tree suffers from black knot disease,","x":0.13377936923038655,"w":0.7867550150553384,"h":0.026627266666970795,"y":0.38519112713882597},{"c":1,"w":0.78275304158528636,"h":0.023417570880640337,"t":"its value for timber decreases, but to a woodworker interested in making bowls, it brings an","x":0.13193245871996367,"y":0.40546558509058417},{"h":0.02065081967743021,"c":1,"t":"opportunity for a unique and beautiful piece of art.","x":0.13382572379697327,"w":0.4332774861653646,"y":0.42674473074125752},{"w":0.75180801391601559,"c":1,"x":0.13186748720022423,"t":"In the past, Pennsylvania landowners were solely interested in the value of their trees as","y":0.45092913530420586,"h":0.02452389726014903},{"h":0.026792040198020062,"y":0.46919042407781442,"t":"high-quality timber. The norm was to remove the stems of highest quality and leave behind","c":1,"x":0.13377712025746766,"w":0.77718358357747397},{"y":0.49080404571117076,"w":0.76913543701171871,"c":1,"x":0.13385156356899841,"h":0.021053561391860209,"t":"poorly formed trees that were not as well suited to the site where they grew. This practice,"},{"c":1,"t":"called 'high-grading'","x":0.1337040807246109,"y":0.51150681604094461,"w":0.18320507049560544,"h":0.020516751488421137},{"h":0.024489591129100985,"c":1,"t":"', has left a legacy of 'low-use wood' in the forests. Some people even","y":0.50760716848623832,"w":0.59850962320963541,"x":0.30850431362490782},{"w":0.73052296956380214,"t":"call these 'junk trees, and they are abundant in Pennsylvania. These trees have lower","x":0.13376732573812736,"y":0.52571081221165417,"c":1,"h":0.025575513037565778},{"h":0.022129942992023199,"c":1,"t":"economic value for traditional timber markets, compete for growth with higher-value","y":0.54713321470432263,"x":0.13577226110992988,"w":0.72649932861328126},{"h":0.026055891565816003,"w":0.76149805704752604,"c":1,"t":"trees, shade out desirable regeneration and decrease the health of a stand* leaving it more","y":0.56150966711760297,"x":0.1338013990967562},{"w":0.78085581461588549,"x":0.13578952152881432,"y":0.58423642929191322,"h":0.021240365096713121,"c":1,"t":"vulnerable to poor weather and disease. Management that specifically targets low-use wood"},{"c":1,"y":0.60301128532879078,"x":0.13579626298792249,"w":0.73423934936523427,"t":"can help landowners manage these forest health issues, and wood energy markets help","h":0.022911637445847899},{"y":0.62630823874767561,"w":0.11657571156819663,"c":1,"t":"promote this.","x":0.13588690170960444,"h":0.016278871197566658},{"y":0.647642452047269,"t":"Wood energy markets can accept less expensive wood material of lower quality than would","c":1,"h":0.024743566780446757,"x":0.13575518705693621,"w":0.77903910319010417},{"c":1,"t":"be suitable for traditional timber markets. Most wood used for energy in Pennsylvania is","y":0.66687220847663475,"h":0.024065129407841113,"w":0.75564107259114577,"x":0.13578263761355289},{"y":0.68706661000469693,"t":"used to produce heat or electricity through combustion. Many schools and hospitals use","h":0.022481570139852303,"x":0.13771954803210748,"w":0.74591812133789059,"c":1},{"t":"wood boiler systems to heat and power their facilities, many homes are primarily heated","x":0.13773411803921845,"y":0.70575274646305242,"h":0.022454612945841834,"w":0.75173690795898451,"c":1},{"t":"with wood, and some coal plants incorporate wood into their coal streams to produce","y":0.72211480359844027,"c":1,"x":0.13767656382800225,"w":0.72461369832356781,"h":0.024288391398492259},{"c":1,"x":0.13769954553421732,"t":"electricity. Wood can also be gasified for electrical generation and can even be made into","y":0.74249493736099925,"w":0.75758112589518234,"h":0.022628598792530652},{"x":0.13771912583286688,"h":0.021960482493367905,"c":1,"y":0.76161600229680471,"t":"liquid fuels like ethanol and gasoline for lorries and cars. All these products are made","w":0.7284467569986981},{"y":0.78046530556100269,"w":0.74011037190755224,"h":0.022732035319010468,"c":1,"x":0.13578218542698275,"t":"primarily from low-use wood. Several tree-and plant-cutting approaches, which could"},{"h":0.022805836044739292,"c":1,"t":"greatly improve the long-term quality of a forest, focus strongly or solely on the use of","x":0.1377449952140741,"y":0.79845658864367475,"w":0.74197987874348958},{"w":0.21002180735270182,"x":0.13774846860526196,"c":1,"y":0.82076103511254994,"t":"wood for those markets.","h":0.016534604461765023},{"t":"* Stand - An area covered with trees that have common features (e.g. size)","w":0.45048543294270832,"y":0.9373831773053517,"x":0.095145632946121592,"c":1,"h":0.010291241559655551},{"y":0.96220930256351767,"x":0.093203883590953551,"w":0.025242718060811367,"t":"20","h":0.014534883112922281,"c":1}],"w":2400}